  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added host-independent low-to-high dense helpers for exact cyclotomic polynomial construction, structural arithmetic, derivatives, field divrem, monic gcd/xgcd, exact roots from split factors or candidates, Sage-compatible formatting, and normalized power-basis serialization. SageMath 10.9.post1 differentials for orders 5 and 12 cover reconstruction, Bezout, factorization, roots, formatting, and coordinates; a CPython Fraction witness proves the source remains ordinary Python. The benchmark records the dynamic baseline before any native lowering.",
    "risks": [
      "Complete cyclotomic factorization is deliberately not reimplemented here; the integration must obtain exact factors from a mature declared resource backend and use dense_roots_from_factorization only for the public root projection.",
      "The helper is not yet wired into ApproximatePolynomialElement, so this commit prepares semantics without changing the current public CyclotomicField(n)[x] surface."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Register src/lib/sagejs/polynomial_algorithms/cyclotomic_core.py in pyrightconfig.json.",
      "Register test/cyclotomic-field-polynomial.cjs in test/node-test-manifest.cjs.",
      "Wire univariate CyclotomicField parents to dense storage and these helpers in polynomial.py; keep factorization as a declared FLINT resource operation.",
      "Use the recorded degree-12 dynamic costs (roughly 15 ms divrem and 85-95 ms gcd/xgcd on linux-x64) to decide which operations need resource-to-resource acceleration."
    ]
  }
